From dcb00beb56d465d8a913a163f2fb9ddb284b4683 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 04:21:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway, gui: the Providers page says the number Claude
 Desktop brackets a model's row with, so a row of that menu can be matched to
 its provider (#2578)

Two providers serving the same Claude model read alike in Claude Desktop's
menu: it names a row after its own catalog and brackets the folded rows
with the ten digits of the id magpie lists the model by (aliasNumber, in
claudeLooking). That number is stable per model, but nothing in magpie
said it, so the user could not tell which provider a menu row is on.

DesktopNumber says the number in the id Desktop is shown a model by, ""
when it is shown the model's own id. providerInfo sends it as `desktop`
on each model the gateway serves (a hand-picked model that isn't served
says none), and the editor draws it as a small badge on the model's chip,
with the words in all four languages.

Run (macOS, darwin arm64, sandboxed HOME with pinned Go caches):
- TestProviderModelsSayDesktopNumber red before (models carried no
  desktop), green after; TestDesktopNumber green
- model-desktop-number.test.cjs (new) red 4/4 on the old app.js, green
  4/4; models-fold, models-free-only, model-rate, model-copy-id,
  model-kind, provider-none-picked, i18n-keys all green, Chromium and
  WebKit, en/zh/de
- TestCoreScriptBudget green (app.js 1,248,015 of 1,250,000)
- gofmt -l clean; go vet ./..., GOOS=linux vet -tags nogui ./...,
  GOOS=windows vet ./...; go build, GOOS=linux build -tags nogui,
  GOOS=windows build

Addresses part of #2578

